{"body":{"matters":"where authority over meaning and action sits","parts":[{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G2000075"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G2000079"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G200007K"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G200007S"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G200007X"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G2000081"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G2000082"}],"prose":"The paper keeps circling one problem: how a whole can act together when its parts keep their own insides, their own vocabularies and their own judgement. Every move it makes, from virtues given bodies to meanings agreed at runtime to a rehearsal in simulation, is a way of binding without absorbing.","title":"Coordinating parts one does not own"},"id":"1M6YBY3G2000074","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000K"]}
